                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="12901409" author="drew.farris" created="Mon, 23 Aug 2010 14:12:25 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looks like this was due to an improper use of the Gram default constructor that happened as a part of the 0.20.2 refactoring work. Does it make any sense to mark things like this, which should only be used by the serialization mechanism inside hadoop, as @deprecated, so that people don&apos;t use them in regular code?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="12901418" author="robinanil" created="Mon, 23 Aug 2010 14:41:00 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Well deprecated has a different meaning doesnt it. Lets wait for the visibility annotations like that used in Hadoop code nowadays.  Dont bother too much at the moment. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="12901449" author="hudson" created="Mon, 23 Aug 2010 15:40:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Integrated in Mahout-Quality #216 (See &lt;a href=&quot;https://hudson.apache.org/hudson/job/Mahout-Quality/216/&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://hudson.apache.org/hudson/job/Mahout-Quality/216/&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;br/&gt;
    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MAHOUT-486&quot; title=&quot;Null Pointer Exception running DictionaryVectorizer with ngram=2 on Reuters dataset&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;MAHOUT-486&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;MAHOUT-486&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Null Pointer Exception running DictionaryVectorizer with ngram=2 on Reuters dataset&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
